    - Production flow: sales rep intakes the order -> master recives a notification saying new order all orders are sorted based on priority -> master assignes a cutting master -> the cutting master sees only the fabric, measurements, due date, priority, and any special instructions (from addons), once done its marked as cutting completed -> if there are any hand works required master assigns a hand-worker -> hand-worker sees the design and location then marks as done -> then master assigns the order to a tailor(tailor sees fabric, measurements, addons ) if no hand work requried a tailour is assigned directly -> onces the tailour is done its handed over to the ironing team and then trial, if any changes requried the alterations are made then the final stiching and ironing process is done and garment is ready for delivery, sales rep then collects the remaining payment or marks it as paylater 




    - Inventory management flow: admin sees all the inventory and plases and order for the requried material and enters a expected delivery date -> once the material is received the warehouse manager scans the barcore which adds the material to the current inventory -> whn a order is placed the warehouse manager sees the coresponding code scans it and despences the requried length which will be updated in the invetory, in case of extra fabric requried the tailors can request the material or the warehouse manager can directly enter the order and dispence the fabric 